description=Two appliances for the kitchen and the yard. The Slow Cooker: a countertop cooker with a removable crock that cooks four times slower than a stove, never burns, and keeps food from spoiling while it's on; throw in any stew ingredients, or cook one of nine Kentucky home-cooking recipes, learned as your Cooking improves or from recipe cards and a booklet. The Brick Smoker: built outdoors with Masonry; feed the firebox wood and load the chamber with meat, poultry or fish, and 8 hours of smoke makes it Smoked (keeps about two weeks), a full day Smoke-Dried (keeps about four months). Smoked meat still goes in stews, and in the crock. Replaces the separate Slow Cooker and Brick Smoker mods.
